1
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:04,375
What are side effects of radiation?

2
00:00:04,916 --> 00:00:06,791
The side effects of radiation

3
00:00:06,791 --> 00:00:10,791
vary depending on what part of your body
is receiving treatment.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,750
There are separate videos
that will go into the specific side

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:17,125
effects of each body side and cancer type,

6
00:00:17,125 --> 00:00:21,500
as well as how to manage and reduce
the symptoms of these side effects.

7
00:00:21,708 --> 00:00:27,041
On a more holistic level, individuals
undergoing radiation may experience fatigue,

8
00:00:27,041 --> 00:00:30,916
such as feeling more tired or
needing a nap when they didn't before.

9
00:00:32,166 --> 00:00:35,750
Some individuals are able
to continue their daily routine,

10
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:40,416
such as going to work,
keeping up with exercise, or going out

11
00:00:40,416 --> 00:00:44,125
while others may need to decrease
their activity level temporarily.

12
00:00:45,625 --> 00:00:47,708
These symptoms are not permanent

13
00:00:47,708 --> 00:00:51,833
and should start to get better with time
after completing treatment.

14
00:00:52,416 --> 00:00:56,666
Some people may have questions
about the long term effects of radiation,

15
00:00:56,666 --> 00:01:00,416
such as the risk of causing
another cancer in the future.

16
00:01:00,583 --> 00:01:04,333
Our modern methods of delivering
radiation are very precise,

17
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:09,750
allowing us to shape the radiation
beam to target only the tumor and reducing

18
00:01:09,750 --> 00:01:15,500
as much as possible the radiation dose
to the surrounding healthy organs.

19
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,791
The risk of developing a secondary cancer

20
00:01:17,791 --> 00:01:21,750
from treatment is very low, less than 1%,

21
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:25,583
and usually takes 15
plus years to develop.

22
00:01:25,791 --> 00:01:29,541
For example, children
receiving radiation are at a higher

23
00:01:29,541 --> 00:01:33,500
risk than individuals
in the latter decades of life.

24
00:01:33,708 --> 00:01:37,458
Additionally, the risk on your health
of declining radiation

25
00:01:37,458 --> 00:01:41,416
treatment to treat the cancer
now is much more dangerous

26
00:01:41,416 --> 00:01:45,458
than the risk of getting another
cancer in 10 to 20 years.
